   "line": [
    "d4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 49,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/3pP3/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "cxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 50,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/3PP3/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "cxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "After the centre is exchanged, Black essentially must play d5 to get a viable game — every other move hands White full control of the centre and a wonderful position.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "In the Alapin, if Black doesn't hit back with d5, White simply owns the centre.",
   "plans": "If Black doesn't play d5, seize the centre with pieces."
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 61,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2np4/8/3PP3/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "d6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The pawn to d6 is a common inaccuracy — it declines the d5 break and cedes the centre. White is already better and can develop with a free hand.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Passing up the freeing break in the Alapin is a real, if quiet, concession.",
   "plans": "Build the centre and develop with tempo."
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 108,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2np4/8/3PP3/2N5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Nc3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Develop the knight to c3 first, not f3 — the knight on f3 would allow the pin with the bishop on g4. There is no reason to hand Black that extra option.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "Choose the developing move that denies the opponent a useful pin.",
   "plans": "Restrict the c8-bishop before committing the king's knight."
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 134.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2np1n2/8/3PP3/2N5/PP3PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 139,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2np1n2/8/3PP3/2N4P/PP3PP1/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "h3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The little pawn to h3 restricts the light-squared bishop, taking g4 away and nudging it toward the far more passive d7-square. A small move with a lasting positional point.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": "A timely h3 denies the bishop its active diagonal and keeps it passive.",
   "plans": "Complete development behind the big centre."
  },
